1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,720
Tesla's newly unveiled Roadster

2
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:03,400
hung upside down on a ramp.

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,120
On another run, it flew off,

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:06,680
rolled upright, and landed.

5
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:08,500
How does a car stick upside down?

6
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,040
Tesla says fans pull air out

7
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:11,440
of the thin gap beneath it.

8
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:12,460
Lower pressure there,

9
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:13,720
normal pressure outside,

10
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:15,020
so the outside air presses

11
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:16,299
the car into the ramp.

12
00:00:16,299 --> 00:00:17,140
Once it's airborne,

13
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:19,360
compressed-gas jets help rotate it upright

14
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:20,400
and hold it steady.

15
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,480
It even cleared a whole row of Teslas,

16
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:23,520
Semi included.

17
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:24,770
Zero to 60?

18
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:27,520
0.81 seconds, by Tesla's own test.

19
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:28,280
And flight?

20
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,880
Tesla lists it only on the invite-only Rocket,

21
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,180
which it says isn't approved for public roads.

22
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:34,500
So the demo flew.

23
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,000
A road-ready flying car?

24
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:36,733
Not yet.
